    {
      "key": "WindowManager",
      "kind": "singleton",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "WindowManager is a singleton that manages all windows in the application",
        "details": "The WindowManager provides a centralized interface for creating, managing, and monitoring windows across the entire application. It follows the singleton pattern to ensure there's only one instance managing all windows, and provides event notifications for various window state changes.\n\nKey features:\n- Singleton pattern ensures single point of window management\n- Event-driven architecture for window state notifications\n- Cross-platform window creation and management\n- Thread-safe access to the singleton instance\n- Automatic cleanup of resources on destruction",
        "notes": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "This class is thread-safe for singleton access, but individual operations may require additional synchronization depending on the platform implementation."
          }
        ]
      },
